    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py` and wrote 47 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. The required command `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. The coverage, CRAP, mutation and bandit gates have not been run; I only ran the tests.\n\nThe query is fully parameterized, and the ORDER BY column and direction come from fixed whitelists, so no user input reaches the SQL text. Substring matching uses `instr(lower(name), lower(?))`, which keeps `%` and `_` literal and folds only ASCII case. Ties are always broken by `id` ascending. The stock filter, inclusive `max_price`, and the `limit`/`offset` ranges are applied as specified. Two choices go beyond the spec: `limit` and `offset` reject `bool` values even though `bool` subclasses `int`, and a non-string `name_contains` raises `ValueError`. The function only runs SELECT statements, and the tests check that the table is unchanged afterward.",
